-- title:
--   Integral q-parameter at the cusp of a ℤ₍ₚ₎-model
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N$, and write $R = \mathrm{GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt}\,p$ for the subring of $\mathbf{Q}$ of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $c : X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be a morphism with $X$ integral, $c$ proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$. The data assumed are: a `CurveModel` $M_0$ over $\mathbf{Q}$ of the field $F_N \subset \mathbf{Q}((q))$ generated by the expansions $j(q^d)$ for $d \mid N$ (an integral scheme, proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf{Q}$, with a $\mathbf{Q}$-isomorphism $\mathrm{ffEquiv}$ of $F_N$ with its function field and a bijection $\mathrm{placeOfPoint}$ from its closed points to the places of $F_N/\mathbf{Q}$ matching stalks with valuation rings), together with an isomorphism $e_0$ of $M_0.C$ onto the generic fibre $X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec}\mathbf{Q}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf{Q}$; a section $\varepsilon_\infty$ of $c$; a closed point $x_0$ of $M_0.C$ whose place is the $q$-adic cusp $\mathrm{cuspInftyFull}\,N$; a $\mathbf{Q}$-point $y$ of the generic fibre which is the restriction of $\varepsilon_\infty$ and whose image under $e_0^{-1}$ is $x_0$; a `CurveModel` $M_\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ of the Laurent base change $\overline{\mathbf{Q}} \cdot F_N$ identified with the geometric generic fibre, with $\mathrm{hgal}$ asserting that its point–place bijection is equivariant for the semilinear $\mathrm{arithmeticGalois}$ action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbf{Q}}/\mathbf{Q})$, and $\mathrm{hcompat}$ asserting that the place of a $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$-point, restricted along $F_N \to \overline{\mathbf{Q}} \otimes_{\mathbf{Q}} F_N \cong \overline{\mathbf{Q}} \cdot F_N$, is the place of the corresponding closed point of $M_0.C$; for each valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, a lift $\rho_A : R \to A$ of $R \to \overline{\mathbf{Q}}$, a `CurveModel` $M_s(A)$ over the residue field $\kappa_A$ of the field generated by the expansions $\bar\jmath(q^d)$, $d \mid N$, identified by an isomorphism with the fibre of $c$ along $\kappa_A$, and, when $\kappa_A$ is algebraically closed, a reduction map $r$ on places satisfying $\mathrm{IsPlaceReductionModL}$ (degrees are preserved, and divisors of Laurent series over $A$ reduce compatibly) which is compatible with specialisation of $A$-valued points of $X$. Finally let $s$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec} R$ with $\{s\}$ closed, and assume the image of $x_0$ in $X$ specialises to $\varepsilon_\infty(s)$. Then, for the $R$-algebra structure on the stalk $S = \mathcal{O}_{X,\varepsilon_\infty(s)}$ induced by $c$, there exist an $R$-algebra map $\pi : S \to R$, an element $t \in S$ and a power series $u \in R[[q]]$ such that the kernel of the stalk map of $\varepsilon_\infty$ at $s$ is contained in $\ker \pi$, $\pi(t) = 0$, $\ker\pi \subseteq (t) + (\ker\pi)^2$, the $q$-expansion of $t$ — its image under specialisation to the generic point, the stalk map of $e_0$ followed by the first projection at $x_0$, passage to the function field and $\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$, viewed inside $\mathbf{Q}((q))$ — equals the image of $u$ in $\mathbf{Q}[[q]]$, and $u$ has zero constant coefficient and unit coefficient of $q$.
--
--   This exhibits a local parameter at the cusp on an integral model of the modular curve whose $q$-expansion is $q$ times a unit plus higher order terms, with coefficients in $\mathbf{Z}_{(p)}$: the formal completion along the cusp section is $\operatorname{Spf} \mathbf{Z}_{(p)}[[q]]$, with $q$ the classical parameter. It feeds the construction of $q$-expansions of sections and differentials on the integral model, being used for the power-series expansion of germs at the cusp and for the identification of $q$-expansions of Kähler differentials up to units.
-- source:
